 [17592186066546 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066546 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066546 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5696f866-cced-54cd-962d-9825c54cd08a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066547 #edb/ref 1080 "-15 < x < 3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066547 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066547 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cc51915d-9f31-5d2b-8475-af5750338981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066548 #edb/ref 1080 "3 < x < 15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066548 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066548 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d1a8075d-79db-5b7f-93ed-6c8f3546511e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066549 #edb/ref 1080 "3 < x < 16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066549 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066549 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ddbc07f0-1a83-5eb5-9ee9-ec2b1a3783cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066550 #edb/ref 1080 "-18 < x < 3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066550 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066550 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ab6de6b-f8b3-567e-990f-a054408be3a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066551 #edb/ref 1080 "3 < x < 18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066551 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066551 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7b367a60-d8d4-5ca7-9ad4-68197390e74f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068472 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13932" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068472 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $0 \\leq 3x+6 < 15.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068472 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0901e241-519b-50ee-ab5f-50b2f631e948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068472 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t0 &\\leq 3x+6 < 15 \\[5pt]\n\t0 - 6 &\\leq 3x + 6 -6 < 15-6 \\[5pt]\n\t-6 &\\leq 3x < 9 \\[5pt]\n\t\\dfrac{-6}{3} &\\leq \\dfrac{3x}{3} < \\dfrac{9}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t-2 &\\leq x < 3\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 \\leq x < 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068473 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13933" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068473 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the inequality $-1 < -2x + 1 \\leq 7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068473 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8208b5ba-8c54-5c05-a9f4-04aa30f8892f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068473 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <-2x+1\\le 7 \\\\ -1-1 & <-2x+1-1\\le 7-1 \\\\ -2 & <-2x\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-2$. However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <-2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{-2} & \\,>\\,\\frac{-2x}{-2}\\,\\ge \\,\\frac{6}{-2} \\\\ 1 & >x\\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $1 > x \\geq - 3,$ but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-3 \\leq x < 1\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068474 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13935" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068474 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution to the inequality $-3 < 1-2x < 11$ using a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f671658-055a-599d-8f1f-416570e604b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068474 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & <1-2x<11 \\\\ -3-1 & <1-2x-1<11-1 \\\\ -4 & <-2x<10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & <-2x<10 \\\\ \\frac{-4}{-2} & >\\frac{-2x}{-2}>\\frac{10}{-2} \\\\ 2 & >x>-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $2 > x > -5$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-5 < x < 2\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/f5/f514a2aca3b3995ea2b1dc970a3b8f16a476ec0f9bb0178909d86ff670503354.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Compound Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068685 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186332976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068686 #edb/ref 1039 "Compound Inequalities Th