ef 1069 "q-3070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069228 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the solution to $-10 < \\frac{6 - 2x}{3} < 0$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069228 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b61c5dfe-34c0-5830-8c59-cd20d813f4bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1061 108821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83b17106-05a3-58df-89b9-4510e4dbee9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069552 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1061 108822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ff1eeef-0d3b-5cde-9aca-5461fbfa7dee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069553 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1061 108825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60d28d8b-03d2-535c-826f-3510ebac457f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1061 108828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5885620e-83f2-528b-862e-d400efe5fd7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality \n\n$$\n4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.\n$$\n\nTo solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate $x.$ Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to *both* the left-hand *and* right-hand sides.\n\nHere, we can isolate $x$ by subtracting $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t4 & \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n\t4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n\t2 &\\le x \\le 6\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $2 \\le x \\le 6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1065 8677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6d8fae47-5e67-5793-a585-d3781d5c4555" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070018 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288306 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288306 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288306 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29233aa0-7f3f-5ec2-b539-ada9fc07a5a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288397 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288397 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288397 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36af17ea-cac8-52c0-92d5-c6ec2922a2c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289104 #edb/ref 1080 "<" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289104 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289104 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a0b2029b-117e-588d-bd5b-c003c19dc8ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289791 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289791 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289791 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289791 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186288397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289791 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1934fb92-eff7-5cc2-80f6-50308250ae74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290026 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290026 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290026 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290026 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186289104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290026 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "87e35e52-a33d-50d1-bef6-7023ece73ad3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290170 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290170 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290170 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290170 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186288306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290170 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca53ce72-d828-5a11-a7a5-e42a6dde34c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1069 "q-214755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the inequality $1<\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$\\,x\\le $\n\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "489f31b9-96a3-50ae-87c4-3a1fc2efa912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290305 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $3$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1 & <3\\cdot \\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & <x+5\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x+5\\le 6 \\\\ 3-5 & <x+5-5\\le 6-5 \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2<x\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
